.TH AGENTX-IFSTACK 8 "September 2026" "agentx-ifstack" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
agentx-ifstack \- serve Linux interface stacks through AgentX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentx-ifstack
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.RB [ \-\-socket " PATH" ]
.br
.B agentx-ifstack
.RB [ \-\-help " | " \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agentx-ifstack
serves the IF-MIB ifStackTable to an SNMP master through an AgentX Unix socket.
Enable
.B master agentx
in snmpd.conf before enabling this service.
.PP
The daemon uses route netlink in its network namespace to find bonds, bridges,
and interface layers.
It serves GET, GETNEXT, and GETBULK requests.
Rows use the higher interface index first and the lower interface index second.
Required zero-index boundary rows are included.
Writes are rejected.
.PP
One process-lifetime monitor subscribes to link notifications before its first
complete inventory.
AgentX reads use only the last published table and never start acquisition.
Periodic reconciliation covers silently missed events.
Before the first valid inventory, or after detected notification loss, reads
return an AgentX processing error until a complete inventory succeeds.
An ordinary inventory failure keeps the previous complete table available.
.PP
The daemon reconnects and registers again when the master disconnects.
Retry delays start at one second and double to a maximum of 30 seconds.
A session that lasts at least 30 seconds resets the delay.
A missing master does not cause the daemon to exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from PATH instead of /etc/agentx-ifstack.toml.
An explicitly selected file must exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Override the socket in the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses TOML and accepts exactly four keys.
Omitted keys use built-in defaults.
An absent default file uses all built-in defaults.
An absent explicit file, malformed TOML, an unknown key, or an invalid value
causes a nonzero exit before any connection attempt.
.TP
.B socket = "/var/agentx/master"
AgentX master Unix socket path.
The path must not be empty.
.TP
.B reconcile = 3600
Seconds between background complete inventories when no link event requires one.
The value must be an integer of at least 1.
.TP
.B priority = 127
AgentX registration priority, from 1 to 255.
Lower values win when registered regions overlap.
.TP
.B log_level = "info"
Default log filter: error, warn, info, debug, or trace.
Logs go to standard error without timestamps.
An idle healthy daemon is quiet at info.
.PP
Override order is built-in defaults, then file values, then command-line flags.
The
.B RUST_LOG
environment variable overrides the log filter.
Restart the process to apply configuration changes.
.SH NON-ROOT OPERATION
The packaged systemd unit runs as root by default.
To configure non-root operation, create a system group and user:
.nf
groupadd \-\-system agentx-ifstack
useradd \-\-system \-\-gid agentx-ifstack \-\-no-create-home \e
    \-\-home-dir /nonexistent \-\-shell /usr/sbin/nologin agentx-ifstack
.fi
.PP
Add this permission directive next to
.B master agentx
in /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf:
.nf
agentXPerms 0660 0755 root agentx-ifstack
.fi
.PP
This directive makes a new AgentX socket mode 0660 and owned by
root:agentx-ifstack.
The socket controls access.
Net-snmp uses the directory mode only when it creates a missing directory.
It does not change the mode of an existing /var/agentx.
If that directory already exists, the administrator must make it traversable
by the agentx-ifstack user.
For example, use mode 0755 when the directory is owned by root:root.
Create /etc/systemd/system/agentx-ifstack.service.d/non-root.conf with this
content:
.nf
[Service]
User=agentx-ifstack
SupplementaryGroups=agentx-ifstack
.fi
.PP
Reload the systemd configuration, restart snmpd.service, and restart
agentx-ifstack.service.
The package container tests start a real master and use setpriv to run the
packaged binary as the agentx-ifstack user.
They verify that it can register and publish rows through the configured
socket.
The containers do not run a service manager.
The tests do not exercise the systemd drop-in, systemd's application of the
supplementary group, or the unit sandbox.
The shipped unit keeps
.BR User=root .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/agentx-ifstack.toml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/agentx/master
Default AgentX master socket.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT terminate the process with their default signal actions.
There is no configuration reload signal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that help or version output completed.
A configuration or command-line error exits with status 1.
During normal operation the process runs until terminated.
Connection and acquisition failures do not terminate it.
.SH NOTES
The service runs as root by default because /var/agentx is normally mode 0700
and owned by root.
An unprivileged process cannot traverse that directory.
The administrator must make an existing directory traversable.
The non-root configuration uses
.B agentXPerms
to control socket access for the agentx-ifstack group.
It uses a systemd drop-in to run the subagent as the agentx-ifstack user.
The systemd unit removes all capabilities and permits Unix and netlink sockets.
It reads the host network namespace directly through netlink.
.PP
Before upgrading from a release that used
.B refresh,
replace that key explicitly in the preserved configuration.
For example, replace
.B refresh = 5
with
.BR reconcile = 3600 .
The removed key is not accepted as an alias.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snmpd.conf (5),
.BR snmpd (8),
.BR rtnetlink (7)
.PP
RFC 2741, Agent Extensibility (AgentX) Protocol Version 1.
.br
RFC 2863, The Interfaces Group MIB.
